---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-command-palette</code> finds and runs commands by name. Give it the commands as data,
  each with an <code>id</code>, a <code>label</code> and optionally a <code>group</code>,
  <code>description</code>, <code>icon</code>, displayed <code>shortcut</code>,
  <code>keywords</code> and <code>disabled</code>. Typing filters them and highlights the match;
  Arrow keys move, Enter runs the command (<code>select</code>), Escape clears the query and then
  closes. <code>shortcut="mod+k"</code> opens it with Ctrl+K, or Command+K on a Mac.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-button id='command-palette-demo-open'>Open command palette (Ctrl+K)</wc-button>
  <wc-command-palette id='command-palette-demo' shortcut='mod+k'></wc-command-palette>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      const palette = document.querySelector('#command-palette-demo');
      palette.commands = [
        { id: 'new-issue', label: 'New issue', group: 'Issues', icon: 'add', shortcut: 'C' },
        { id: 'assign', label: 'Assign to me', group: 'Issues', icon: 'person', shortcut: 'I' },
        { id: 'close-issue', label: 'Close issue', group: 'Issues', icon: 'check', keywords: ['resolve', 'done'] },
        { id: 'inbox', label: 'Go to inbox', group: 'Navigation', icon: 'inbox', shortcut: 'G+I' },
        { id: 'settings', label: 'Open settings', group: 'Navigation', icon: 'settings', description: 'Account and workspace preferences' },
        { id: 'billing', label: 'Billing', group: 'Navigation', icon: 'credit_card', disabled: true, description: 'Only admins can open billing' },
        { id: 'theme', label: 'Toggle dark theme', group: 'Preferences', icon: 'dark_mode', keywords: ['appearance'] },
      ];
      palette.recent = ['settings'];
      document
        .querySelector('#command-palette-demo-open')
        .addEventListener('click', () => palette.show());
      palette.addEventListener('select', event => {
        const { id } = event.detail.command;
        palette.recent = [id, ...palette.recent.filter(other => other !== id)].slice(0, 3);
        myConsole.log(`select: ${id}`);
      });
      palette.addEventListener('close', event => {
        myConsole.log(`close: ${event.detail.reason}`);
      });
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Recent commands</h3>
<p>
  While the query is empty, the commands whose ids are in <code>recent</code> come first, under
  "Recent". The palette does not keep the list itself: update it on <code>select</code> and store
  it where the app keeps preferences.
</p>

<h3>Shortcut</h3>
<p>
  <code>shortcut</code> takes modifiers and a key joined by <code>+</code>: <code>mod</code>
  (Command on Apple platforms, Ctrl elsewhere), <code>ctrl</code>, <code>meta</code>,
  <code>shift</code> and <code>alt</code>, for example <code>mod+shift+p</code>. It is ignored while
  the person types in another field, and pressing it again closes the palette. A command's own
  <code>shortcut</code> is only displayed; the app binds it.
</p>
